{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_transport_cwc_3d_ppm",
    "description": "Three-dimensional consistency with continuity (CWC) for the MONOTONE PPM scheme on the latlon3d grid at 12x7x9 -- the free-stream-preservation gate for the PRODUCTION reconstruction, as opposed to its donor-cell sibling latlon3d_transport_cwc_3d (the same model with upwind1_flux rules). Carries the AIR MASS (m) alongside the TRACER MASS (mq) and derives q = mq/m, so six rules fire in one model: three bare-D face-flux-divergence rules closing continuity (lon periodic, lat polar, lev no-flux) and three compound MONOTONE PPM flux-form advection rules carrying the tracer. The winds are shape-disjoint (Mx over [lon_nodes,lat,lev], My over [lon,lat_nodes,lev], Mz over [lon,lat,lev_nodes]) against q over [lon,lat,lev], so the esm-spec 9.6.1 shape constraints select each rule unambiguously.\n\nTHE PROPERTY UNDER TEST (MEASURED). At q == 1 every CW84 slope is a difference of equal values and is therefore EXACTLY 0.0 in IEEE; the edge value collapses to 0.5*(1+1) + (1/6)*(0 - 0) = 1 exactly; the monotone limiter leaves aL = aR = 1, so the parabola is the constant 1 and its integrated donor-region average is exactly 1. The face flux is then F = max(w,0)*1 + min(w,0)*1 = M bitwise, so each compound divergence collapses onto its bare-D continuity twin to the last bit, dmq/dt equals dm/dt exactly, and q stays EXACTLY 1. Measured 2026-07-16: dev = 0.0 exactly at t=0 and t=0.1 (Linf, atol 1e-12). NOTE this is a DIFFERENT argument from the donor case's (F = 0.5*(M*(1+1) - |M|*(1-1)) = M); the donor's proof does NOT carry over to PPM and must not be cited here.\n\nNON-VACUITY. The assertion reference is the CONSTANT ZERO, so a 0.0 result would pass even if dev were dead. problems/_falsifier_ppm3d.esm is this problem with ic(mq) multiplied by 1.000001 (q = 1+1e-6); it drives dev to 1.08e-6 at t=0.1 and correctly FAILS, which is what makes this gate meaningful. It is regenerated from this file plus the perturbation -- if you change this problem, re-run the falsifier. Only the t=0.1 assertion discriminates: dev is a state integrated from dev(0)=0, so its t=0 value is 0.0 by construction even under perturbation.\n\nMESH. NLAT=7 is the FLOOR for the monotone lat rule (three cap rows at each pole plus a non-empty interior). NLON=12 and NLEV=9 give those axes a genuine mid-domain interior rather than the all-boundary degenerate case N=7 produces. The property is bitwise exactness and is resolution-independent; build cost tracks stencil width, not cell count, so 12x7x9 (756 cells) builds no slower than 7x7x7 (343). Costs ~370 s / ~3.5 GB, dominated by the monotone PPM build (esm-spec 9.7.3 inlines template bodies and the Expression AST has no let/sharing node, so the reconstruction chain re-inlines each stage into the next), not the solve.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "op:D",
      "axes:lon,lat,lev",
      "scheme:flux_form",
      "property:free_stream"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "TransportCWC3dPPM": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lon_periodic.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lat_polar.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lon_mono_periodic.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lat_mono_polar.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 12,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 9
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "m": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air mass per cell (a pressure thickness). Strictly positive."
        },
        "mq": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Tracer mass per cell. Initialised bitwise equal to m, so q == 1."
        },
        "dev": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Diagnostic deviation dev = mq - m, obtained by integrating the DIFFERENCE of the two right-hand sides from dev(0) = 0. This is the quantity the conformance assertion gates: at q == 1 the tracer divergence collapses bitwise onto the continuity divergence, so dev's own right-hand side is EXACTLY 0.0 in IEEE and dev never leaves zero. It exists because assertion `reference` expressions are build-time and cellwise and cannot read states or observeds, so q itself is not assertable and asserting mq would require re-spelling the entire discrete divergence by hand -- i.e. duplicating the operator inside its own test. Against a constant-zero reference there is nothing for the test to get wrong. dev feeds nothing back into m or mq."
        },
        "lon0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Grid's lon0_deg free name; 0 closes the periodic zonal circle."
        },
        "lat0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": -90.0,
          "description": "Grid's lat0_deg free name; -90 for the pole-to-pole global recipe."
        },
        "dlon_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              360.0,
              12
            ]
          },
          "description": "Zonal spacing 360/NLON = 360/12 = 30 deg, closing the periodic zonal circle. Spelled as a LITERAL because NLON is pinned at the expression_template_imports edge and is therefore consumed there -- a metaparameter bound at an import edge is not a live name in the importing document's scope (esm-spec 9.7.6). Keep this in sync with the NLON binding above by hand."
        },
        "dlat_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              180.0,
              6
            ]
          },
          "description": "Meridional spacing 180/(NLAT-1) = 30 deg, pole-to-pole endpoint-inclusive; NLAT = 7 is the FLOOR for the monotone lat rule (three cap rows at each pole plus a non-empty interior). Spelled as a literal for the same import-edge reason as dlon_deg."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical edge coordinate, uniform on [0,1], monotone increasing with lev (k=1 is the SURFACE). The divisor is NLEV = 9; keep it in sync with the NLEV binding above by hand (same import-edge reason as dlon_deg).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "kn"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "kn": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    "kn",
                    1
                  ]
                },
                9
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thicknesses from the grid's lev_thickness template.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lev_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "pe": "pe"
            }
          }
        },
        "zc": {
